ve_order_number=13054; citation 62 FR 36965; document_number 97-18288; field disposition_notes","sha256":"8ba9e1cce593bb06b6be625b585b15bb04a1555ed34ad8c5b6f8c9bd81f83f77","url":{"characters":590,"preview":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bcorrection%5D=0&conditions%5Bpresidential_document_type%5D=executive_order&conditions%5B","sha256_utf8":"d136bbd46dbf384a5a7f7e191405abcdeb476b9adbc9e10d1abc6539fa76c008","truncated":true}},{"page_or_item":"OFR API record executive_order_number=13062; citation 62 FR 51755; document_number 97-26364; field disposition_notes","sha256":"8ba9e1cce593bb06b6be625b585b15bb04a1555ed34ad8c5b6f8c9bd81f83f77","url":{"characters":590,"preview":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/documents?conditions%5Bcorrection%5D=0&conditions%5Bpresidential_document_type%5D=executive_order&conditions%5B","sha256_utf8":"d136bbd46dbf384a5a7f7e191405abcdeb476b9adbc9e10d1abc6539fa76c008","truncated":true}}],"summary":"See complete record at pointer"}],"notice":"Research startup packet; statuses remain provisional. Overflow records are explicit and require their source pointers.","overflow":{"claim_draft":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"f5c2b79a90ea23df5a78422c9776ea7beb3ab2eb3030156ecf1f3fa738ee1899"},"conflicts":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945"},"current_law_hits":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"98100b1f90b7710324ce53a6f0b1175c2bfa58eeccb09e07de320d5b64762a39"},"fragments":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"dc3126bd945e21ee7b34894dbc60b87d832f071052367ac661d98bbbcd493e5a"},"later_events":{"reason":"30 KB startup budget; follow record pointers for complete evidence","sha256":"2ffc42209d426745790dbc44861c273f3725103b58fdd6d98df5dd5b4c2372b3"}},"readiness":{"blockers":"CLAIM_INCOMPLETE:clause_inventory|CLAIM_INCOMPLETE:ending_or_current_basis|CLAIM_INCOMPLETE:savings_residuals","claim_present":"yes","claim_record_errors":"unresolved_material_gaps","decision_origin":"inherited_legacy_v2","exhausted_steps":"","instrument_id":"EO:13054","provisional_status":"yes","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"done","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"n/a","step_original_text":"done","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"6","steps_done":"3"},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"no current-law lead is checked through 2026-10-14 (U.S. Code entries are current only through 2026-10-09); confirm the last days by hand"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"yes","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"By the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the laws of the United States of America, including sections 3301 and 3302 of title 5 and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, and in order to permit certain overseas employees to acquire competitive status upon returning to the United States, it is hereby ordered as follows:\n\nSection 1. A United States citizen who is a family member of a Federal civilian employee and who has separated from Federal service to accept employment with the American Institute in Taiwan pursuant to section 11 of Public Law 96-8 (93 Stat. 18, 22 U.S.C. 3310(a)) may be appointed noncompetitively, in accordance with Executive Order 12721 and implementing regulations of the Office of Personnel Management, to a competitive service position in the executive branch, provided such family member meets the qualifications and other requirements established by the Director of the Office of Personnel Management, including an appropriate period of satisfactory overseas employment with the American Institute in Taiwan.\n\nSec. 2. The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall prescribe such regulations as may be necessary to implement this order.\n\nSec. 3. This order shall be effective upon publication in the Federal Register.\n\nWilliam J. Clinton\n\nThe White House,\n\nJuly 7, 1997.\n\n[Filed with the Office of the Federal Register, 8:45 a.m., July 9, 1997]\n","path":"jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-13054-eligibility-certain-overseas-employees-for-noncompetitive.txt","sha256":"ce3b2e7a033c93f5ffa734a98fc198c1ca2f19fdc93f272024db8bfbd85f5727","source":{"line":3093,"path":"jobs/app-transcriptions/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"41a628d188c14c37f3d52fb665515d0bf523463daa964d3ab9392c97d54f6d59"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 13054 of July 7, 1997\nEligibility of Certain Overseas Employees for Noncompetitive\nAppointments\nBy the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the\nlaws of the United States of America, including sections 3301 and 3302\nof title 5 and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, and in\norder to permit certain overseas employees to acquire competitive status\nupon returning to the United States, it is hereby ordered as follows:\nSection 1. A United States citizen who is a family member of a Federal\ncivilian employee and who has separated from Federal service to accept\nemployment with the American Institute in Taiwan pursuant to section\n11 of Public Law 96–8 (93 Stat. 18, 22 U.S.C. 3310(a)) may be appointed\nnoncompetitively, in accordance with Executive Order 12721 and implement-\ning regulations of the Office of Personnel Management, to a competitive\nservice position in the executive branch, provided such family member\nmeets the qualifications and other requirements established by the Director\nof the Office of Personnel Management, including an appropriate period\nof satisfactory overseas employment with the American Institute in Taiwan.\nSec. 2. The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall prescribe\nsuch regulations as may be necessary to implement this order.\nSec. 3. This order shall be effective upon publication in the Federal Register.\nœ–\nTHE WHITE HOUSE,\nJuly 7, 1997.\n[FR Doc. 97–18288\nFiled 7–9–97; 8:45 am]","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-13054-f551c51ab6.txt","sha256":"69d4e5b670e4d8700df26310cc8fd76241a585b8a6024cd37853610a7fce4234","source":{"line":8382,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"606d17181661637f986886f77e0fdfd5789d8e3670a8f1866826495302c03d1b"}},{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"text\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\\nEx. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by the Impoundment Control Act of 1974 (Public Law 93–344; 88 Stat. 332, (2 U.S.C. 681 et seq.), hereinafter referred to as the Act) [subchapters I and II of this chapter], and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, the Director of the Office of Management and Budget is hereby designated and empowered to exercise, as of October 1, 1974 without ratification or other action of the President (1) the functions required by sections 1014(b) and 1014(d) of the Act [subsecs. (b) and (d) of this section] of transmitting to the Comptroller General of the United States and to the Office of the Federal Register copies of special messages transmitted pursuant to section 1012 or 1013 (2 U.S.C. 683 and 684) of the Act; and (2) the function conferred upon the President by section 1014(e) of the Act (2 U.S.C. 685","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"5b6e5de61be4ea9c9c4749827c02d0c9d484107505b7e9adae3172a42351c188"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:13054\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1997-07-10/pdf/97-18288.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: f551c51ab61a149d4c6ccfd08e58bc6e170d38544f82e0f2a9529daa9925add9\nLocation: 62 FR 36965, PDF pages 1-1 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 1 ===\nPresidential Documents\n36965\nFederal Register\nVol. 62, No. 132\nThursday, July 10, 1997\nTitle 3—\nThe President\nExecutive Order 13054 of July 7, 1997\nEligibility of Certain Overseas Employees for Noncompetitive\nAppointments\nBy the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the\nlaws of the United States of America, including sections 3301 and 3302\nof title 5 and section 301 of title 3 of the United States Code, and in\norder to permit certain overseas employees to acquire competitive status\nupon returning to the United States, it is hereby ordered as follows:\nSection 1. A United States citizen who is a family member of a Federal\ncivilian employee and who has separated from Federal service to accept\nemployment with the American Institute in Taiwan pursuant to section\n11 of Public Law 96–8 (93 Stat. 18, 22 U.S.C. 3310(a)) may be appointed\nnoncompetitively, in accordance with Executive Order 12721 and implement-\ning regulations of the Office of Personnel Management, to a competitive\n","path":"j